carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nFirst, let's factor out the coefficient next to the $x$ inside the function:\n\n$$\ny=7f(2x-2)+5=7f(2(x-1))+5\n$$\n\nTo get $y=7f(2(x-1))+5,$ we could apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}4).$ Stretch $y=f(x)$ by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}=0.5$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(2x).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}3).$ Translate $y=f(2x)$ right by $1$ unit to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(2(x-1)).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}2).$ Stretch $y=f(2(x-1))$ by a scale factor of $7$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=7f(2(x-1)).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}1).$ Translate $y=7f(2(x-1))$ up by $5$ units to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=7f(2(x-1))+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a possible order of transformations is\n\n$\\,$ $(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}2)\\to (\\text{T}1).$"] ["question-56fcd68f-be15-5bdd-9b31-95eea95afa89" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-014d1aa7-6876-598e-b36b-73f23d2e7df3" :answer-field/id #uuid "014d1aa7-6876-598e-b36b-73f23d2e7df3"] ["answer-b047744c-b2e2-51d7-b12c-1fa93bce8cb4" :answer/id #uuid "b047744c-b2e2-51d7-b12c-1fa93bce8cb4"] ["answer-b047744c-b2e2-51d7-b12c-1fa93bce8cb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b047744c-b2e2-51d7-b12c-1fa93bce8cb4" :answer/value "(\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)\\to (\\text{T}1)"] ["answer-9130b0d1-296f-54fe-866a-5d9499a8522f" :answer/id #uuid "9130b0d1-296f-54fe-866a-5d9499a8522f"] ["answer-9130b0d1-296f-54fe-866a-5d9499a8522f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9130b0d1-296f-54fe-866a-5d9499a8522f" :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}2)"] ["answer-0db0e1b6-b15e-5702-b4eb-23afbb278ad9" :answer/id #uuid "0db0e1b6-b15e-5702-b4eb-23afbb278ad9"] ["answer-0db0e1b6-b15e-5702-b4eb-23afbb278ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/